# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every checkout gets LF working-tree bytes, including Windows. Without this,
# git on Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true` and rewrites the working tree
# to CRLF on checkout, which fails Biome's LF-only formatter on every file that
# it checks — 605 errors on the first windows-latest quality-gate run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Access/VBA sources round-trip byte-for-byte between the repository and the
# Access binary. Git must never rewrite their line endings: the semantic
# classifier and the binary-sync read-back compare these bytes directly, so a
# platform-dependent conversion would show up as phantom drift.
*.bas -text
*.cls -text
*.frm -text
*.form.txt -text
*.form.json -text

# Binary artifacts.
*.accdb binary
*.laccdb binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
